[{:seon.task/name "a-shard-says-what-each-test-waits-on"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by the stability sweep of 2026-10-25 (docs/failure-points.md; the owner: platform stability first). test side of the sweep (target/waits-test.md in the stability worktree): bin/test waits on its shards in index order (bin/test's wait $P[i]), so a hung shard 1 hides later shards' output; and test waits with no end beyond their answer: ts/ask's socket read of a live parked root (test/seon/test_store.clj:202), start-root!'s wait for ROOT LISTENING (167), stop-root! (207), kill-root! (178), binary-sh of a mode that parks (113), agent_test's and e2e's <!! event loops on an events tap (agent_test.clj:51,82,133,176,349,365,388; e2e.clj:81,236) that skip a dead agent's event, check.clj's await-event with no terminal event named (204,496,510,517,745,980,1156), bare @p / <!! after a synchronous step in procs_test (282-372), problems_test:176, step_test:11-20 (use the answer helper, procs_test.clj:466, or realized?). Correct: bin/test reports each shard as it ends (wait -n), and each test wait names its end: an agent's or root's death event ends an event loop (a loop that skips a death is red), a synchronous step's answer is read with realized? (no wait). The parked-everywhere case is jolt.async/a-process-whose-every-thread-parks-ends-its-waits. Clocks in test (check.clj:879,984,1001,649,1473,67,1135; lib_test.clj:50,81,84) are listed in target/waits-test.md for docs/clocks.md's owner to name or remove."
  :seon.task/kind :work}
 {:seon.task/name "a-process-test-costs-its-boots-not-its-work"
  :seon.task/plan "Measured 2026-11-06 (docs/testing.md#a-root-costs-what-it-boots): bin/test --all was 1,931 s of tests serial, 9.5 min on 4 shards, 42 tests of 15 s or more being 73 percent of it; they did 2-9 M ticks and waited on root boots. Causes found: in-agent gave its shared root source dirs [\"src\"], so seon.program/required! could not load main's test namespaces through the AOT cache and the fork server evaluated 2,274 forms at its first fork (11.6 s a root, 1.9 s with the config's dirs), and one root per distinct dirs; main-is-proved-at-boot ran all 1,152 tests main held for two verdicts (183 s to 12 s on a store of its own); root-threads-are-what-root-declares ran three process cycles bin/check lifecycle repeats (82 s to 24 s); stores of a test's own imported the checkout and the wiki to prove a store resumes (27 s to 11 s). Done: those four (commits 752525deb9, 39fbccb1fb). Open: one shared root per distinct :sets in agent-test (a tuned root for child-min-ms, jobs, node-cache-bytes, heap-extra-bytes serves them all: 7 s a variant a shard); own-root agent tests whose subject is not the root's life can use the shared root; the root's boot (5 s, about 3 s of it not yet attributed) and the fork server's first fork (2.7 s) are the floor of every process test."
  :seon.task/kind :work}]
